  https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f
PersonalClaw: distinguish dormant skill catalog from autonomous execution
  https://github.com/PersonalClaw/PersonalClaw

PUBLICATION AND SAFETY INVARIANTS
---------------------------------
I1. PRIVATE stays out of export-public, including edges to private parents.
I2. Evidence labels do not substitute for experimental verification.
I3. A correction remains explicit; don't silently overwrite an earlier claim.
I4. The audit chain detects accidental editing and unchained modification,
    NOT a malicious actor capable of rewriting the entire file and all hashes.
I5. No external service calls, autonomous agent actions, background tasks,
    chat capture, or unattended deployment occur in this implementation.
I6. Don't feed hidden/private lineage to a blind-reconstruction test.
I7. Every source and user correction requires attribution and review before
    PUBLIC release; visibility='public' is *not* automatic authorization.
I8. Unobserved intent is unknown, not an invitation to invent testimony.

EVENT MODEL
-----------
{
  "id": "stable-identifier",
  "kind": "artifact|intent|correction|rejection|constraint|reframe|skill|test|observation",
  "text": "atomic assertion or instruction",
  "source": "README.md#... or authorized chat note / experiment identifier",
  "visibility": "public|private",
  "status": "specified|fixture-tested|independently-verified|deployed",
  "parents": ["event-id"],
  "evidence": ["test or other specific record id"],
  "tags": ["topic", "operator"],
  "created": "UTC ISO-8601 timestamp"
}
Status values are DECLARED labels. A local validator requires specific evidence
for high-status declarations, but does not independently adjudicate truth.

COMMANDS
--------
